concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-2-sec-6-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6(3) Application of Australian criminal law outside the adjacent area"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-6-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The substantive criminal law of the Jervis Bay Territory, as in force from time to time, is taken to have applied at sea outside the adjacent area to a criminal act:  (a) on a foreign ship; or  (b) in the course of activities controlled from a foreign ship; or  (c) of a person who has abandoned, or temporarily left, a foreign ship and has not returned to land; if the first country at which the ship calls, or the person lands, after the criminal act, is Australia or an external territory of Australia." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The substantive criminal law of the Jervis Bay Territory, as in force from time to time, is taken to have applied at sea outside the adjacent area to a criminal act:  (a) on a foreign ship; or  (b) in the course of activities controlled from a foreign ship; or  (c) of a person who has abandoned, or temporarily left, a foreign ship and has not returned to land; if the first country at which the ship calls, or the person lands, after the criminal act, is Australia or an external territory of Australia."@en ;
