doc:sch-1-sec-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4 Evidentiary presumption about the locus of an offence" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If, in proceedings for a maritime offence, an alleged act, omission or state of affairs, that is an element of the offence, is proved, an allegation in the information or complaint that the act, omission or state of affairs happened in the adjacent area, inner adjacent area, or outer adjacent area for a particular State is taken to be proved in the absence of proof to the contrary.  The cooperative scheme  Schedule 1 The intergovernmental agreement  Part 3  Clause 5  Crimes at Sea Act 2000 Compilation date: 30/8/19 Registered: 2/9/19" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-1-sec-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5 Intergovernmental agreement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-5 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commonwealth Attorney-General, on behalf of the Commonwealth, and the participating State Ministers may enter into an agreement providing for the division of responsibility for administering and enforcing the law relating to maritime offences.  (2) The intergovernmental agreement may provide for concurrent responsibility in specified parts of the adjacent area." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commonwealth Attorney-General, on behalf of the Commonwealth, and the participating State Ministers may enter into an agreement providing for the division of responsibility for administering and enforcing the law relating to maritime offences.  (2) The intergovernmental agreement may provide for concurrent responsibility in specified parts of the adjacent area."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "68219b5106893bad2dc3ed4e22a54678e2990dc6fd62c7b178a5c0a5a9382a7c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "25"^^xsd:integer ;
