concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-1-sec-12 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12 Regulations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-12 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Governor-General may make regulations prescribing matters:  (a) required or permitted by this scheme to be prescribed; or  (b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this scheme.  (2) However, a regulation affecting the operation of this scheme in relation to the inner adjacent area for a State may only be made with the agreement of the participating State Minister for the relevant State.  The cooperative scheme  Schedule 1 Adjacent areas  Part 6  Clause 13  Crimes at Sea Act 2000 Compilation date: 30/8/19 Registered: 2/9/19" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Governor-General may make regulations prescribing matters:  (a) required or permitted by this scheme to be prescribed; or  (b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this scheme.  (2) However, a regulation affecting the operation of this scheme in relation to the inner adjacent area for a State may only be made with the agreement of the participating State Minister for the relevant State.  The cooperative scheme  Schedule 1 Adjacent areas  Part 6  Clause 13  Crimes at Sea Act 2000 Compilation date: 30/8/19 Registered: 2/9/19"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4aeff976b8f4c71c6f63eebd40b9867f98b47f62774e5e374c19bb6fb9f91a70" ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer ;
