    skos:prefLabel "14(2) Adjacent areas"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-14-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The adjacent area for Queensland is:  (a) so much of the area described in Schedule 1 to the Offshore Petroleum and Greenhouse Gas Storage Act 2006 (Commonwealth) in relation to Queensland as is within the outer limits of the continental shelf; and  (b) the Coral Sea area (within the meaning of subsection 8(2) of the Offshore Petroleum and Greenhouse Gas Storage Act 2006 (Commonwealth)) other than the territorial sea within the Coral Sea area; and  (c) the areas within the outer limits of the territorial sea adjacent to certain islands of Queensland as determined by proclamation on 4 February 1983 under section 7 of the Seas and Submerged Lands Act 1973 (Commonwealth); and  (d) the space above and below the areas described in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The adjacent area for Queensland is:  (a) so much of the area described in Schedule 1 to the Offshore Petroleum and Greenhouse Gas Storage Act 2006 (Commonwealth) in relation to Queensland as is within the outer limits of the continental shelf; and  (b) the Coral Sea area (within the meaning of subsection 8(2) of the Offshore Petroleum and Greenhouse Gas Storage Act 2006 (Commonwealth)) other than the territorial sea within the Coral Sea area; and  (c) the areas within the outer limits of the territorial sea adjacent to certain islands of Queensland as determined by proclamation on 4 February 1983 under section 7 of the Seas and Submerged Lands Act 1973 (Commonwealth); and  (d) the space above and below the areas described in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)."@en ;
